   "format": "mcq",
   "stem": {
      "text": "Find the radius of convergence of the power series \\( \\sum_{n=1}^{\\infty} \\frac{(x+1)^{2n}}{9^{n}(2n+1)} \\)."
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "symbolic",
      "mathjson": 3
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "For the ratio test, \\( \\left|\\frac{a_{n+1}}{a_n}\\right| = \\frac{\\left(\\frac{2 n}{9} + \\frac{1}{9}\\right) \\left|{x + 1}\\right|^{2}}{2 n + 3} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Divide",
            [
               "Multiply",
               [
                  "Power",
                  [
                     "Abs",
                     [
                        "Add",
                        "x",
                        1
                     ]
                  ],
                  2
               ],
               [
                  "Add",
                  [
                     "Divide",
                     [
                        "Multiply",
                        2,
                        "n"
                     ],
                     9
                  ],
                  [
                     "Rational",
                     1,
                     9
                  ]
               ]
            ],
            [
               "Add",
               [
                  "Multiply",
                  2,
                  "n"
               ],
               3
            ]
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "As \\( n \\to \\infty \\), the limit of this ratio is \\( \\frac{\\left|{x + 1}\\right|^{2}}{9} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Divide",
            [
               "Power",
               [
                  "Abs",
                  [
                     "Add",
                     "x",
                     1
                  ]
               ],
               2
            ],
            9
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "The series converges when \\( \\frac{\\left|{x + 1}\\right|^{2}}{9} < 1 \\), that is, when \\( \\left|x + 1\\right| < 3 \\).",
         "mathjson": 3
      },
      {
         "step": 4,
         "text": "The radius of convergence is \\( R = 3 \\).",
         "mathjson": 3
      }
   ],
